15:30.820 --> 15:33.050
<b>Help out some, Aizawa Ayumu.</b>

15:34.150 --> 15:35.190
<b>With what?</b>

15:35.190 --> 15:36.520
<b>Can’t you tell from looking?</b>

15:37.720 --> 15:38.890
<b>Okay.</b>

15:49.740 --> 15:51.070
<b>So, how did it feel?</b>

15:51.640 --> 15:54.540
<b>There’s no shade around here, so... hot.</b>

15:54.540 --> 15:56.910
<b>Oh, ho... I see, I see.</b>

15:57.940 --> 16:01.050
<b>Not that! I’m talking about when 
you were with Wakkun.</b>

16:01.050 --> 16:03.050
<b>How much do you know?</b>

16:05.250 --> 16:06.780
<b>You stopped being able to meet him, right?</b>

16:07.520 --> 16:08.790
<b>What do you think of that?</b>

16:08.790 --> 16:12.220
<b>Wakkun’s waited too long.</b>

16:12.220 --> 16:15.360
<b>Before he met you, and after meeting you, too.</b>

16:15.360 --> 16:16.230
<b>And?</b>

16:16.230 --> 16:18.700
<b>I’m the one asking the questions here!</b>

16:18.700 --> 16:20.530
<b>How did it feel?</b>

16:20.530 --> 16:22.700
<b>The day before last, 
I couldn’t go see him.</b>

16:22.700 --> 16:24.840
<b>When I went yesterday,
 he wasn’t there.</b>

16:24.840 --> 16:28.310
<b>It felt like l did something I couldn’t take back...</b>

16:28.310 --> 16:30.040
<b>He wasn’t there today, either...</b>

16:30.040 --> 16:33.740
<b>While stressing out on what to do about
this, I managed to cool off a little.</b>

16:34.610 --> 16:36.110
<b>But now, everything’s already...</b>

16:36.110 --> 16:38.180
<b>You’re really a good person, aren’t you?</b>

16:38.180 --> 16:40.150
<b>No, I’m not.</b>

16:40.150 --> 16:43.690
<b>Ayumu, why did you become so frantic over this?</b>

16:47.260 --> 16:48.730
<b>Because Wakkun was waiting for me...</b>

16:48.730 --> 16:51.700
<b>...just like I was waiting for him before...</b>

16:53.430 --> 16:55.200
<b>You’ll be fine, Ayumu.</b>

16:55.200 --> 16:56.200
<b>Everyone’s watching over you.</b>

16:56.700 --> 16:57.840
<b>Everyone?</b>

17:01.510 --> 17:03.370
<b>Everyone is everyone.</b>

17:16.620 --> 17:18.090
<b>Thank you very much.</b>

17:18.820 --> 17:21.660
<b>When the timing’s a little more convenient,
 I’ll direct Mikoshiba-san your way.</b>

17:21.660 --> 17:22.990
<b>Yes, thank you.</b>

17:34.940 --> 17:38.080
<b>Is this world’s membrane becoming thinner today?</b>

17:38.080 --> 17:39.210
<b>More or less, I suppose.</b>

17:40.580 --> 17:44.150
<b>It’s just that you seem to have a habit of saying that.</b>

17:44.150 --> 17:46.150
<b>A habit of saying it, huh?</b>

17:46.150 --> 17:48.520
<b>It’s no good if it’s become my pet saying...</b>

17:51.320 --> 18:01.030
<b>Kishiro Animal Hospital</b>

18:05.400 --> 18:07.070
<b>So you’re the doctor’s son?</b>

18:08.410 --> 18:09.610
<b>What’s the matter?</b>

18:09.610 --> 18:13.110
<b>It looks like you’ve had your shirikodama
 taken by a kappa.</b>

18:13.110 --> 18:14.950
<b>Kappas don’t exist.</b>

18:14.950 --> 18:16.380
<b>“Kappa’s don’t exist...”</b>

18:16.380 --> 18:17.050
<b>Is that so?</b>

18:18.520 --> 18:19.450
<b>They don’t.</b>

18:19.450 --> 18:23.520
<b>You only think they don’t... 
thus you profess that they don’t exist.</b>

18:24.220 --> 18:25.720
<b>How interesting.</b>

18:28.760 --> 18:34.170
<b>This world is far more rich, complicated,
 and fragile than people think.</b>

18:34.170 --> 18:38.100
<b>Mister... do you have ESP or something?</b>

18:38.640 --> 18:41.140
<b>Having ESP is nothing more than a feeling.</b>

18:41.140 --> 18:43.570
<b>It’s an impression one gets, or a feeling
one reads from the atmosphere.</b>

18:43.580 --> 18:46.580
<b>I have no interest in something ambiguous like that.</b>

18:47.450 --> 18:51.820
<b>People need to gather data and analyze the
phenomena, then think about the results.</b>

18:54.650 --> 19:00.360
<b>All that has happened and all that
will happen has meaning.</b>

19:00.360 --> 19:03.660
<b>This is a necessary process people must go through.</b>

19:03.660 --> 19:05.630
<b>At least, that’s what I believe.</b>

19:12.240 --> 19:14.570
<b>Heigorou-san stopped by today, right?</b>

19:15.210 --> 19:16.370
<b>Yes, he did.</b>

19:16.380 --> 19:19.440
<b>You told me there were a lot
of rumors about him, right?</b>

19:19.440 --> 19:21.050
<b>Could you give me an example?</b>

19:24.280 --> 19:27.280
<b>It’s just that his dog Roku has become
attached to me recently...</b>

19:27.290 --> 19:30.320
<b>...so we end up talking sometimes.</b>

19:30.320 --> 19:32.420
<b>They’re just rumors.</b>

19:32.420 --> 19:33.490
<b>Yeah.</b>

19:34.730 --> 19:36.530
<b>I guess there are three patterns associated with him...</b>

19:37.400 --> 19:39.400
<b>One is that he’s a retired college professor.</b>

19:39.400 --> 19:41.670
<b>Another is that he’s a retired non-fiction writer.</b>

19:41.670 --> 19:42.500
<b>Or, he’s a wanderer who always fits in.</b>

19:43.140 --> 19:44.940
<b>A wanderer who always fits in...?</b>

19:44.940 --> 19:47.100
<b>You didn’t know him before you came here...</b>

19:47.110 --> 19:50.470
<b>...but since you met him, you can talk
to him like it was nothing, right?</b>

19:50.980 --> 19:53.210
<b>Which do you think he is?</b>

19:53.210 --> 19:54.880
<b>Who knows?</b>

19:54.880 --> 19:57.950
<b>It might end up that he’s actually none of them.</b>

19:57.950 --> 20:00.650
<b>Ah, that reminds me, Junko...</b>

20:00.650 --> 20:02.650
<b>Your mother wanted you to give her a call.</b>

20:03.920 --> 20:06.890
<b>You and Mom still keep in touch?</b>

20:08.260 --> 20:10.630
<b>Well, you’re here...</b>

20:10.630 --> 20:12.860
<b>...and your mother tends to worry, so...</b>

20:13.430 --> 20:15.000
<b>I see...</b>

20:15.000 --> 20:16.330
<b>I guess that makes sense.</b>

20:17.300 --> 20:20.710
<b>It seems we’ve really gotten a lot of interesting, complicated information...</b>

20:20.710 --> 20:22.310
<b>...coming from the district of Asahi in Yokohama.</b>

20:22.310 --> 20:24.110
<b>In the countryside, right?</b>

20:24.110 --> 20:25.110
<b>Ah, yes.</b>

20:25.110 --> 20:26.120
<b>Apparently,</b>

20:26.120 --> 20:29.480
<b>there have been a lot of eyewitnesses 
saying they’ve seen UFOs around there.</b>

20:29.480 --> 20:30.820
<b>And what’s so complicated about that?</b>

20:30.820 --> 20:32.320
<b>Supposedly, they’re really tiny!</b>

20:32.320 --> 20:35.320
<b>Like jumbo-sized fireflies, or corpse candles,
or something like that.</b>

20:35.320 --> 20:38.290
<b>Then couldn’t they really be some
big fireflies or corpse candles?</b>

20:38.290 --> 20:42.060
<b>I don’t know, but fireflies normally
just look pretty around rivers...</b>

20:42.060 --> 20:43.660
<b>...and corpse candles are usually in cemeteries, right?</b>

20:43.660 --> 20:46.900
<b>But these were supposedly spotted
around a residential area, so...</b>

20:46.900 --> 20:50.940
<b>Ah, so since they were unidentified flying
objects, that would make them...</b>

20:50.940 --> 20:51.940
<b>...UFOs!</b>

20:51.940 --> 20:53.270
<b>Right?</b>

21:03.210 --> 21:04.210
<b>Aizawa Junko</b>

21:04.210 --> 21:05.680
<b>Aizawa Junko</b>

21:07.990 --> 21:08.650
<b>Hello?</b>

21:08.650 --> 21:10.390
<b>How are you doing?</b>

21:10.390 --> 21:11.360
<b>Okay...</b>

21:11.360 --> 21:13.560
<b>I asked that man to tell you I called...</b>

21:13.560 --> 21:14.460
<b>I heard.</b>

21:14.460 --> 21:17.430
<b>If you heard,
 why didn’t you give me a call?</b>

21:17.430 --> 21:19.430
<b>Sorry. I had a lot of things to do.</b>

21:20.530 --> 21:22.430
<b>I trust you’re okay then, right?</b>

21:22.430 --> 21:23.270
<b>Yeah.</b>

21:23.270 --> 21:25.700
<b>Umm... I just got out of the bath...</b>

21:25.700 --> 21:29.640
<b>...and I haven’t dried off my head yet,
so could I call you back in a bit?</b>

21:29.640 --> 21:33.310
<b>Ah, yeah. Be careful 
not to catch a cold, okay?</b>

21:33.310 --> 21:34.350
<b>I’ll be fine.</b>

21:34.350 --> 21:35.680
<b>Well then, talk to you soon.</b>

21:36.620 --> 21:37.720
<b>Ah, wait!</b>

21:37.720 --> 21:38.980
<b>Yes?</b>

21:38.980 --> 21:41.090
<b>I’m going to ask you something weird, but...</b>

21:41.090 --> 21:43.420
<b>Mom, when you came here 
with me last time...</b>

21:43.420 --> 21:44.320
<b>To Tana?</b>

21:44.320 --> 21:49.090
<b>Yeah. Do you remember seeing a boy wearing
a poncho and rubber boots back then?</b>

21:50.530 --> 21:51.230
<b>What’s so funny?</b>

21:51.230 --> 21:55.230
<b>Well of course I do.
There’s no way I’d forget.</b>

21:55.230 --> 21:56.430
<b>What kind of boy was he?</b>

21:57.400 --> 21:59.240
<b>A very cute one.</b>

21:59.240 --> 22:00.340
<b>“Cute”?</b>

22:00.340 --> 22:02.670
<b>Ayumu, don’t you remember?</b>

22:02.670 --> 22:03.410
<b>No...</b>

22:03.940 --> 22:05.940
<b>That... was you.</b>

22:13.750 --> 22:17.490
<b>Back then, you loved your poncho
and rubber boots so much...</b>

22:17.490 --> 22:20.090
<b>...that you were always wearing them.</b>

22:21.560 --> 22:23.460
<b>Ayumu? Can you hear me?</b>

22:24.760 --> 22:26.800
<b>Hello? What’s the matter?</b>

22:52.250 --> 22:59.820
Daremo shiranai kotoba de kimi he to

22:52.250 --> 22:59.820
On that nostalgic hill, I sang out to you

22:59.820 --> 23:06.530
Utaikaketa natsukashii oka de

22:59.820 --> 23:06.530
words that no one else knew.

23:09.530 --> 23:17.030
Tomare soyokaze kawaranu omoide

23:09.530 --> 23:17.030
The dying breeze and my unchanged memories

23:17.030 --> 23:23.710
Sotto misete ano koro no boku wa

23:17.030 --> 23:23.710
gently reveal to me what I was like back then.

23:23.710 --> 23:31.150
Aa yume wo aishite hitori ni natta

23:23.710 --> 23:31.150
Ah, I thought that being alone

23:31.150 --> 23:35.950
Sore de ii to omotta

23:31.150 --> 23:35.950
and cherishing my dream would be fine.

23:35.950 --> 23:44.630
Haruka na sora ni wa ima mo kimi ga iru darou

23:35.950 --> 23:44.630
I wonder if you’re still there right now in the distant sky?

23:44.630 --> 23:53.230
Yasashiku ikiru yo afureru namida koraeta

23:44.630 --> 23:53.230
Now I lead a simple life, having suppressed my overflowing tears.

23:53.230 --> 24:02.010
Mirai no melody ga shizuka ni yureru kisetsu

23:53.230 --> 24:02.010
The melody of the future is in the quietly stirring seasons.

24:02.010 --> 24:10.720
Aitai na itsu no hi ka... mattete

24:02.010 --> 24:10.720
I want to see you again, and I’m waiting for that day.

24:10.720 --> 24:19.260
Aitai ne boku wa mada humming boy

24:10.720 --> 24:19.260
I want to see you again, but I’m still a humming boy.

24:19.980 --> 24:22.980
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

24:20.450 --> 24:24.780
<b>Ah! You went and ate my meat
again without asking, Rokkun!</b>

24:24.780 --> 24:25.420
<b>Munch.</b>

24:25.420 --> 24:26.280
<b>What did you say?!</b>

24:26.280 --> 24:31.360
<b>Give me back my precious meat!
I got it from Nene-chan!</b>

24:31.360 --> 24:32.390
<b>Munch, munch.</b>

24:32.390 --> 24:34.730
<b>A girl shouldn’t be so loud over meat!</b>

24:34.730 --> 24:36.130
<b>Why don’t you just eat some vegetables?</b>

24:36.130 --> 24:37.660
<b>I need my meat!</b>

24:37.660 --> 24:39.660
<b>Eight parts meat, two parts vegetables.</b>

24:39.660 --> 24:41.900
<b>And of course, desserts count completely different.</b>

24:41.900 --> 24:45.140
<b>You fool! If you eat like that, your stomach’s
membrane will grow thinner!</b>

24:45.140 --> 24:50.440
<b>What? I don’t really get what you just said,
but anyway, eat more vegetables, Taruto!</b>

24:50.440 --> 24:51.580
<b>Aww...</b>

24:51.580 --> 24:54.410
<b>I’ll ask Heigorou-san to prepare some
of his home-grown veggies for you.</b>

24:54.410 --> 24:57.650
<b>Next time: “The World’s Membrane Grows Thinner.”</b>

24:55.010 --> 24:59.950
<b>The World’</b>s Membrane Grows Thinner
